{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3172","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3172","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3172\",\"parent_revision\":\"6f3b2db43c0007edf23a9f4a31ebfa68480a20faf17e552e8ea80de18d78e6ed\",\"root_revision\":\"6f3b2db43c0007edf23a9f4a31ebfa68480a20faf17e552e8ea80de18d78e6ed\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nuv run plugins/development-harness/tests/run_pytest.py reports 5096 passed, 2 failed on a tree whose only changes are markdown and YAML. Both reproduce in isolation and are unrelated to that work.\\n\\nFailure 1 \u2014 backlog_core/tests/unit/progressive_markdown/test_indexer_decomposition.py::TestPLRLintGate::test_indexer_build_passes_plr_complexity_gates\\n\\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'ruff'\\n\\nThe test shells out via subprocess.run to a bare 'ruff'. run_pytest.py is a PEP 723 self-resolving script whose environment does not provide a ruff binary, so the test cannot run under the standalone runner at all. This is the runner path AGENTS.md documents for running the plugin's suites, so the PLR complexity gate is effectively never enforced there. Fix by declaring ruff in the runner's dependency block, or by invoking it through the same uv-managed environment the rest of the suite uses, rather than assuming a host-global binary.\\n\\nFailure 2 \u2014 tests_backlog/test_github_sync_provider.py::test_github_content_provider_replay_preserves_concurrent_remote_revision\\n\\nAssertionError: assert 'queued' == 'revision-two'\\n\\nAfter replaying a queued mutation against a concurrently-updated remote, the provider returns the queued content where the test expects the newer remote revision to be preserved. Either the replay path clobbers a concurrent remote revision, or the test encodes an intent the provider no longer implements. Determine which before changing either side.\\n\\nReproduce:\\n  uv run plugins/development-harness/tests/run_pytest.py backlog_core/tests/unit/progressive_markdown/test_indexer_decomposition.py::TestPLRLintGate::test_indexer_build_passes_plr_complexity_gates -q --no-cov\\n  uv run plugins/development-harness/tests/run_pytest.py tests_backlog/test_github_sync_provider.py::test_github_content_provider_replay_preserves_concurrent_remote_revision -q --no-cov\\n\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **two pre-existing failures in the development-harness standalone test runner** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed while running quality gates for PR #3168\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2e84c28e042cb8552a78f75ee106fbed58ee863e9325aea41ed3afdd91b30715\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQOH19g\"}"}